{"abstract":"In-service teachers' professional development (PD) courses on digital education tend to be based on a restrictive idea of ‘knowledge transfer’ presupposing an application of course content into practice through a top-down and linear approach. In this paper, we adopt a broader conceptual perspective to examine the learning outcomes of an online/hybrid PD course developed through a design-based research project between 2020 and 2023 and attended by 98 participants from four Higher Education institutions in Denmark. We draw on the cultural-historical activity theory concepts of ‘recontextualisation’ and ‘construction/instantiation’ of the object of activity to analyse interviews with course participants (n = 15). The main findings reveal how the teachers engaged with the resources they encountered in the course to reshape their teaching practices by personalising these resources and adapting them to situated concerns. We identified three types of resources (knowledge, tools, and networks) that the teachers recontextualised to achieve transformation of their practices. This transformation happened in two ways: by reconstructing and remediating problem spaces in teaching, and by bringing about concrete solutions to both existing and newly formulated challenges. In this process, peer feedback and collective discussions were essential elements of the teachers' learning process. In conclusion we discuss the broader relevance of our findings for designing and evaluating online and hybrid digital education PD courses.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Popov, Jelena","Pischetola, Magda","Poderi, Giacomo","Møller, Jeppe Kilberg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828771"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University College London"],"keyword":["Cultural Historical Activity Theory","Digital education","Higher education","Learning outcomes","Recontextualisation","Teacher professional development"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"it opened a new teaching space for me transforming higher education practice through digital education","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.lcsi.2025.100922","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828771","identifier":[{"id":"105010123636","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-428f76ac-07fe-4602-9382-2e2d84c2a94d"],"keyword":["Cultural-historical activity theory","Digital education","Higher education","Learning outcomes","Recontextualisation","Teacher professional development"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-64CF97CC3DEE126859FD3BE53A72672C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/463374553/2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.lcsi.2025.100922","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University College London","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Jelena","key":"popovpau","last":"Popov","name":"Popov, Jelena","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Magda","key":"pischetolapau","last":"Pischetola","locid":"227e791f-6e3e-410c-afd5-0c6dcb56aab9","name":"Pischetola, Magda","orcid":"0000-0001-6697-2118","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Giacomo","key":"poderipau","last":"Poderi","name":"Poderi, Giacomo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jeppe Kilberg","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Jeppe Kilberg","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.lcsi.2025.100922","issn":["22106561"],"journal":"Learning, Culture and Social Interaction","paperid":"100922","status":"p","title":"Learning, Culture and Social Interaction","volume":"53"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105010123636"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-428f76ac-07fe-4602-9382-2e2d84c2a94d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"‘It opened a new teaching space for me’ : Transforming higher education practice through digital education","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828771","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"This study moves from the research question: how to design a professional course/concept for the development of higher education teachers’ digital competences? It presents Teknosofikum, a project funded by the Danish Ministry of Higher Education and Science between 2020 and 2023. The outcome of the project is a course for higher education teachers with a focus on digital competence. Grounded in sociomaterial theories, digital competence refers here to the capacity to develop agency towards professional changes driven by technology. It comprises teachers’ abilities to evaluate why, when, how and with what effects to include digital technologies in teaching. The study draws on qualitative and quantitative data gathered through design-based research along the first three course iterations, with a total of 64 participants. The findings show the emergence of three design principles: (i) relational approach to technology; (ii) praxis; and (iii) organized non-linearity. These principles will guide the final format of Teknosofikum course/concept.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pischetola, Magda","Møller, Jeppe Kilberg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-486461"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"design principles for higher education teacher development the teknosofikum course concept","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7146/lom.v15i27.134151","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-486461","ids":["ku-9b996135-e2dd-4542-9f59-1478b144987e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-4367F5380AAA2FB90C880BEF9DFB088A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7146/lom.v15i27.134151","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/337294645/Pischetola_M_ller_2023_Design_principles_for_Higher_Education_teacher_development.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Magda","key":"pischetolapau","last":"Pischetola","locid":"227e791f-6e3e-410c-afd5-0c6dcb56aab9","name":"Pischetola, Magda","orcid":"0000-0001-6697-2118","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jeppe Kilberg","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Jeppe Kilberg","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.7146/lom.v15i27.134151","issn":["1903248X"],"issue":"27","journal":"Læring og Medier","pages":"1-40","status":"p","title":"Læring og Medier","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9b996135-e2dd-4542-9f59-1478b144987e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Design principles for higher education teacher development : the Teknosofikum course/concept","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-486461","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Professional development programs for teachers in higher education are often characterized by top-down approaches, which fail to make appreciable differences in teaching practices. This study uses a qualitative approach to explore activity-oriented design (AOD) as an instrument for collaborative learning in higher education teacher professional development. We examine Teknosofikum, an ongoing project developed in Denmark along three iterations, involving a total of 64 course participants (42 in the hybrid format; 22 online). The study applies the methodology of design-based research: data was collected via 15 semi-structured group interviews, online forums, and field notes/recordings from online meetings and onsite workshops. Data analysis follows the methodology of grounded theory and evidence is given significance inductively, based on contextual data. Four activities were selected to assess the potential of AOD methods in enhancing teacher collaboration, with different aims: reflection, discussion, theory-practice alignment, and participation. Our analysis revolved around three main categories: trust, deep interaction, and shared beliefs/values. The results show how collaborative group work activities have improved trust and knowledge-sharing among participants and have contributed to creating a safe learning environment. The paper concludes that AOD methods could better assist educational designers in promoting professional development courses that aim at enhancing teacher collaboration in higher education.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Pischetola, Magda","Møller, Jeppe Kilberg","Malmborg, Lone"],"cuid":["S02-099.05-681507"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Activity oriented design","Collaborative learning","Higher education","Teacher professional development"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enhancing teacher collaboration in higher education the potential of activity oriented design for professional development","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10639-022-11490-x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.05-681507","identifier":[{"id":"36532797","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85143330077","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9735077","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["itu-650c97b6-ba36-4fe2-933d-f933ccd9b20e","ku-a6e8f53d-8782-4f06-ae64-c2ccd1de9cc8"],"keyword":["Activity-oriented design","Collaborative learning","Higher education","Teacher professional development"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-531A2845C6DE472DD01DDF8ACE67BC60"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10639-022-11490-x","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://eur02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Frdcu.be%2Fc033u&data=05%7C01%7Cm.pischetola%40hum.ku.dk%7C5d443a544abb4828eaa308dad739d8ff%7Ca3927f91cda14696af898c9f1ceffa91%7C0%7C0%7C638058940694383776%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&sdata=syTV48G%2Fr8%2BOh2D51sXEjyLz2lZgrJ%2Bvm6Q76X%2BNlI0%3D&reserved=0","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102674604/s10639-022-11490-x.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9735077/pdf/10639_2022_Article_11490.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s10639-022-11490-x.pdf?pdf=button","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Magda","key":"pischetolapau","last":"Pischetola","locid":"227e791f-6e3e-410c-afd5-0c6dcb56aab9","name":"Pischetola, Magda","orcid":"0000-0001-6697-2118","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeppe Kilberg","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"0309c0d2-f64d-4449-a321-e39e8fba9f83","name":"Møller, Jeppe Kilberg","orcid":"0000-0001-5851-191X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lone","key":"malmborgpau","last":"Malmborg","name":"Malmborg, Lone","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36532797"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10639-022-11490-x","issn":["13602357","15737608"],"issn_org":["13602357"],"journal":"Education and Information Technologies","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Education and Information Technologies","volume":"2022"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85143330077"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-650c97b6-ba36-4fe2-933d-f933ccd9b20e","ku-a6e8f53d-8782-4f06-ae64-c2ccd1de9cc8"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Enhancing teacher collaboration in higher education : the potential of activity-oriented design for professional development","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.05-681507","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Most cancer treatments today take place in outpatient clinics; however, it might be necessary for some patients to be admitted to hospital departments due to severe side effects or complications. In such situations, support from family and social relations can be crucial for the patients' emotional well-being. Many young adolescents and children whose parents have cancer describe how they are not seen, heard, or listened to as the worried relatives they are. Within the intensive care unit, it has been recommended that early supportive interventions are tailored to include children of the intensive care patient; a similar approach might be relevant in the oncological setting. To our knowledge, no studies have explored how to involve young relatives who are visiting their parent at an oncological department. Recently, a framework for developing theory-driven, evidence-based serious games for health has been suggested. Such a process would include stakeholders from various disciplines, who only work toward one specific solution. However, it is possible that bringing together different disciplines, such as design, art, and health care, would allow a broader perspective, resulting in improved solutions. Objective: This study aims to develop tools to enhance the social interaction between a parent with cancer and their child when the child visits the parent in the hospital. Methods: In total, 4 groups of design students within the Visual Design program were tasked with developing games addressing the objective of strengthening relations in situ during treatment. To support their work, the applied methods included professional lectures, user studies, and visual communication (phase I); interviews with the relevant clinicians at the hospital (phase II), co-creative workshops with feedback (phase III), and evaluation sessions with selected populations (phase IV). The activities in the 4 phases were predefined. This modified user design had the child (aged 4-18 years) of a parent with cancer as its primary user. Results: Overall, 4 different games were designed based on the same information. All games had the ability to make adults with cancer and their children interact on a common electronic platform with a joint goal. However, the interaction, theme, and graphical expression differed between the games, suggesting that this is a wide and fertile field to explore. Conclusions: Playing a game can be an efficient way to create social interaction between a parent with cancer and a child or an adolescent, potentially improving the difficult social and psychological relations between them. The study showed that the development of serious games can be highly dependent on the designers involved and the processes used. This must be considered when a hospital aims to develop multiple games for different purposes.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Piil, Karin","Gyldenvang, Helle Holm","Møller, Jeppe Kilberg","Kjoelsen, Tine","Juul, Jesper","Pappot, Helle"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-026691"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Piil, Karin"],"keyword":["Adolescents","Cancer patients","Children","Emotional well being","Gamification","Relatives","Serious games","Social relation","Visual design"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"electronic games for facilitating social interaction between parents with cancer and their children during hospitalization interdisciplinary game development","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/16029","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-026691","identifier":[{"id":"85100235591","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33475523","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7861993","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-c10a0e27-3508-4847-955c-869093032861","ku-f6cbf364-b47a-4a5f-a7d7-94bd025fb20f"],"keyword":["Adolescents","Cancer patients","Children","Emotional well-being","Gamification","Relatives","Serious games","Social relation","Visual design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F3E4F00E889FE876160860CEC5F5F958"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/256630036/PDF_4_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/16029","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Department of Science in Nursing, Emdrup"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Karin","key":"piilpau","last":"Piil","locid":"a4276db9-c68a-403f-857b-57772bd02312","name":"Piil, Karin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Helle Holm","key":"gyldenvangpau","last":"Gyldenvang","name":"Gyldenvang, Helle Holm","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeppe Kilberg","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Jeppe Kilberg","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Tine","key":"kjoelsenpau","last":"Kjoelsen","name":"Kjoelsen, Tine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","name":"Juul, Jesper","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Helle","key":"pappotpau","last":"Pappot","locid":"e87e8def-c55b-42dc-bef5-763375d59d76","name":"Pappot, Helle","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33475523"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2196/16029","issn":["22919279"],"issue":"1","journal":"JMIR Serious Games","paperid":"e16029","publisher":"JMIR Publications Inc.","status":"p","title":"JMIR Serious Games","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85100235591"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c10a0e27-3508-4847-955c-869093032861","ku-f6cbf364-b47a-4a5f-a7d7-94bd025fb20f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Electronic games for facilitating social interaction between parents with cancer and their children during hospitalization : Interdisciplinary game development","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-026691","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
